Pages = {589-608},
Month = {APR 3},
Abstract = {The article applies the concept of democratic resilience to recent
   political developments in Europe. In line with core definitions of the
   concept, we distinguish between ways in which European democracy has
   resisted crises and threats, on the one hand, and deeper democratic
   renewal, on the other hand. In each of these categories, we assess
   institutional, societal and transnational resilience. Disaggregating
   resilience in this manner helps pinpoint both the achievements and
   limitations of European democratic resilience.},
